Id: fsys019e
Severity: ERROR
Category: filesystem
Check: find_files

Auditing a system that is not running (tigris --root), its files are
scanned with this host's find, and that scan needs GNU find: its
-fprintf writes each kind of finding (setuid, setgid, devices, links,
world-writable directories, unowned files) to its own list in one pass,
and only that pass can judge ownership by the image's passwd and group
and find dangling links inside the image. This find (busybox's, most
likely) has no -fprintf, so the image's files were not scanned at all.

Install GNU findutils on the host doing the audit, or audit from one
that has it.
